1
00:00:00,130 --> 00:00:02,930
Your AI agent might just be a workflow in disguise. One question decides it.

2
00:00:03,130 --> 00:00:06,930
In a workflow, you draw the steps. They're fixed in code, cost and latency are predictable, and it's easy to test.

3
00:00:07,130 --> 00:00:12,930
In an agent, the model picks the steps. That buys flexibility, but cost varies per request and you have to evaluate the whole path, not just the answer.

4
00:00:13,130 --> 00:00:21,930
Use an agent only when the steps can't be known in advance, wrong actions are reversible or gated, the flexibility is worth variable cost, and you can evaluate the whole trajectory. Otherwise, build the workflow and add AI at the steps that need judgment.

5
00:00:22,130 --> 00:00:26,930
Draw it first. If you can, skip the agent. Share this with your AI product team.
